attus norvegicus", "R. norvegicus", "Rn", "brown rat", "Norway rat"], "taxId": "10116", "abbreviation": "RNO", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "transition", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}, {"dbId": 10055507, "displayName": "PKC-delta phosphorylates CARD9", "stId": "R-MMU-5607740", "stIdVersion": "R-MMU-5607740.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["PKC-delta phosphorylates CARD9"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Mus musculus", "inferredFrom": [5607740], "species": [{"dbId": 48892, "displayName": "Mus musculus", "name": ["Mus musculus", "M. musculus", "Mm", "house mouse"], "taxId": "10090", "abbreviation": "MMU", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "transition", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}], "reviewed": [{"dbId": 5621625, "displayName": "Geijtenbeek, Teunis B H, 2014-09-02", "dateTime": "2014-09-02 13:22:43", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}], "species": [48887], "summation": [{"dbId": 5607610, "displayName": "Activation of NF-kB signaling is a critical event downstream...", "text": "Activation of NF-kB signaling is a critical event downstream of CLEC7A (Dectin-1), CLEC6A (Dectin-2) (Bi et al. 2010) and CLEC4E (Mincle) (Yamasaki et al. 2008), requiring the adapter protein Caspase recruitment domain (CARD)-containing protein 9 (CARD9) in dendritic cells and in macrophages (Gross et al. 2006, Hara et al. 2007). CARD9 is analogous to CARD-containing MAGUK protein 1 (CARMA1), which mediates T-cell receptor (TCR) activation of NF-kB in lymphocytes. CARD9 is downstream of SYK and becomes phosphorylated by PRKCD (Protein  kinase C-delta) phosphorylates CARD9 on Thr-231 (T231), which is required for the signal-induced association of CARD9 with B-cell lymphoma 10 (BCL10) and  Mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue 1 (MALT1) and the subsequent recruitment of MAP3K transforming growth factor beta activated kinase 1 (TAK1), leading to activation of the NF-kB pathway (Strasser et al. 2012). A homozygous loss-of-function mutation in human CARD9 results in a premature termination codon (Gln295*).  Patients with this mutation are highly susceptible to fungal infections (Glocker et al. 2009).", "literatureReference": [5607202, 5607401, {"dbId": 5621490, "displayName": "CARD9 mediates dectin-2-induced IkappaBalpha kinase ubiquitination leading to activation of NF-kappaB in response to stimulation by the hyphal form of Candida albicans", "title": "CARD9 mediates dectin-2-induced IkappaBalpha kinase ubiquitination leading to activation of NF-kappaB in response to stimulation by the hyphal form of Candida albicans", "journal": "J. Biol. Chem.", "pages": "25969-77", "pubMedIdentifier": 20538615, "volume": 285, "year": 2010, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20538615", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 741423, "displayName": "Card9 controls a non-TLR signalling pathway for innate anti-fungal immunity", "title": "Card9 controls a non-TLR signalling pathway for innate anti-fungal immunity", "journal": "Nature", "pages": "651-6", "pubMedIdentifier": 16862125, "volume": 442, "year": 2006, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16862125", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 5607254, "displayName": "A homozygous CARD9 mutation in a family with susceptibility to fungal infections", "title": "A homozygous CARD9 mutation in a family with susceptibility to fungal infections", "journal": "N. Engl. J. Med.", "pages": "1727-35", "pubMedIdentifier": 19864672, "volume": 361, "year": 2009, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19864672", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five st